id faber
name Faber
appeared 2026
creators Ian Zepp
tags pl
website https://faberlang.dev
latestVersion v1.17.0
lab https://github.com/faberlang
fileExtensions fab
description Faber (Faber Romanus) is an experimental, statically typed language designed to be written by language models and read by people. Every operator is a single glyph with one meaning, types come before names, and failure is a typed second channel. The same analysed program can be rendered in several reader languages (English, Latin and others). A reference interpreter defines the semantics, and code generators emit Rust, Go, TypeScript, Swift, Python, C and LLVM IR, each measured against it. Experimental through version 1.x.
writtenIn rust
compilesTo rust go typescript swift python c llvmir wgsl racket

docs https://faberlang.dev/en-US/
isOpenSource true
fileType text
country United States
twitter https://twitter.com/faberlang
domainName faberlang.dev
reference https://agentlanguages.dev/languages/faber/

example
 fn greet(string name) → string {
     return "Salve, §!"(name)
 }
 
 fn divide(int a, int b) → int ⇥ string {
     if b ≡ 0 then throw "division by zero"
     return a / b
 }
 
 main {
     let list<string> names ← ["Ana", "Ben"]
     for from names let name {
         print greet(name)
     }
     print divide(7, 0) ⊥ -1
 }

githubRepo https://github.com/faberlang/faber

